catalysts:
- commercial launch, pricing and third-party validation of DYNAMIXEL-Q and AI Sapiens;
- named design wins with unit volumes, actuator content and repeat paid orders;
- sustained double-digit operating margins after the compensation charge;
- conversion of elevated inventory and Uzbekistan capacity into cash-generative sales;
- continued North American, European and Chinese export growth; and
- evidence that open-source adoption produces recurring hardware, service or data revenue.

- fiscal-2026 adjusted EBITDA guidance delivered with improving quarterly cash conversion;
- selling-price increases catching input-cost inflation without material volume loss;
- Electrical adjusted EBITDA margin stabilising and then recovering;
- data-centre, utility, and electrical-infrastructure volume remaining positive; and
- proceeds and cost savings from portfolio simplification reducing net leverage.

- production reaches targeted levels early in fiscal 2027 and delayed revenue converts without
  further working-capital build;
- consecutive positive operating-cash-flow quarters and declining contract/inventory intensity;
- backlog conversion with stable or rising normalised gross margin;
- data-centre awards converting into profitable revenue; and
- warranty and project-cost revisions remaining contained.

- US sell-through stabilising sequentially without additional channel inventory;
- battery shipments and attach rates growing at healthy gross margin;
- Q2 revenue landing above the midpoint with less dependence on safe-harbour shipments;
- tariffs declining or pricing and domestic production offsetting their margin impact;
- European growth broadening and commercial products converting into recurring demand; and
- sustained free cash flow after normalising tax-credit monetisation and working capital.
